> **3.3A No in-place update of a helper (owner, 21 November 2026).** An installed helper is never overwritten, whether
> or not the change would alter results. A helper found to be wrong is corrected by a new file (`..._v2.py`) and a
> **successor variant** for each variant that used it; the old variants are withdrawn by the owner (section 11) and
> their markers removed in DEV. The successors are new variants and begin their own place in the prevailing OV-1. Code
> that is expected to keep improving without changing any result belongs in the infrastructure (12.4), which can be
> updated under its "nothing may change" check.
> 
114a124,128
> - **Three DEV conveniences** (owner; they touch nothing outside DEV). `Who_Uses.bat <helper>` lists every variant whose
>   declaration names that helper. `Make_Successors.bat <old helper> <new helper>` copies each such variant to a new
>   folder with the next version number in its name and rewrites its helper reference and declaration; it marks
>   nothing, and the owner reviews the result. `Make_Installable.bat` accepts several variants at once, and
>   `--unmark` removes markers.
